.TH IF 1.SH NAMEif \- conditional execution for shell procedures.SH SYNOPSIS\fBif\fR[not] condition [argument ...] commands [else commands] endif.SH DESCRIPTION\fBif\fRtests a condition and hands the commands after it -- or, if thecondition is false, the commands after\fBelse\fR-- to the shell to run.  The conditions:.TP 12\fBdef\fI var\fRthe environment variable\fIvar\fRis defined..TP 12\fBloaded\fI module\fR\fImodule\fRis in memory..TP 12\fBvarval\fI var value\fR\fIvar\fRhas the value\fIvalue\fR.\fR.PP\fBnot\fRbefore the condition turns it round..nf    if loaded runb bio else echo "load runb first" endif.fiIt runs the chosen commands through a module called\fBshell\fR,\fRthe one your own OS-9 brings, and without one resident nothing runs.Under bash,\fBif\fRis a reserved word:\fBcommand if\fRreaches this one..SH SEE ALSOgen, run, mexist